id: pm-gh1390
title: "GH-1390: Keep trusted merge-receipt attribution and committed reconciliation authoritative"
description: The report describes receipt-attributable drift routed to history-repair and a reconciled durable receipt treated as pending by another worktree. Reproduce with real shared Git worktrees before modifying the reconciliation contract.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T11:45:54.908Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T08:52:33.045Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T08:52:32.284Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T08:52:32.284Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Trusted pending receipt overlap routes drift remediation to merge reconcile; Committed reconciled state dominates stale clone-local pending indexes; Repeated reconciliation writes nothing and adds no duplicate audit event; Unrelated drift and malformed evidence remain fail-closed.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Trustworthy bounded context and SDK-owned evidence
value: Agents can act on one truthful context read and preserve durable evidence
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Require exact immutable receipt provenance and complete sealed verified merge_reconcile disposition before accepting durable terminal state. Reuse identical audits only from reanchored verified sealed history; matching unsealed legacy context receives a new sealed event while preserving its original entry. Keep readonly scans, correct health attribution and idempotent interrupted retries."
expected_result: "Committed audited settlement dominates stale local copies, unaudited or mismatched evidence stays pending without writes, and legacy unsealed retry context is recovered once through a sealed audit with unchanged repeat history."
actual_result: "40 linked cases and all 9884 applicable tests pass with exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage. Complete strict static and four TypeScript projects pass. Nine packed npx/bunx packages and installed Node/Bun conflict-abort, legacy audit recovery, byte-preservation and typed-preview-refusal journeys pass. Both actionable CodeRabbit findings were reproduced before their fixes; final pushed-head hosted checks and full re-review remain landing gates, with publication awaiting the next eligible daily release."
affected_version: 2026.10.4
